# PharmaFlow AI Cursor Rules

You are working on PharmaFlow AI, a pharmacy-focused outbound calling SaaS demo.

## Project Context

- Repo: `/Users/manitdankhara/Projects/pharmaflow-ai`
- GitHub: `https://github.com/manit0700/pharmaflow-ai`
- Frontend: React, Vite, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn-style/Radix components
- Backend: Express, TypeScript, Prisma
- Local DB: SQLite
- Production target: Vercel
- Real-call integration: Twilio Voice
- Optional AI call mode: OpenAI
- Production URL: `https://pharmaflow-ai.vercel.app`

## Core Commands

- Run local app: `npm run dev:pc`
- Kill old API ports: `npm run api:kill-old`
- Build all: `npm run build`
- Build server only: `npm run build --prefix server`
- Deploy production: `npx vercel@latest deploy --prod --yes`
- Check production health: `curl https://pharmaflow-ai.vercel.app/api/health`

## Current Product Areas

- `/dashboard`: live call jobs and manual patient entry
- `/calls`: polished Call Recordings dashboard with mock call review data
- `/conversations`: call history/transcripts from jobs
- `/workflows`: call flow/demo
- `/analytics`: call analytics
- `/compliance`: demo compliance dashboard

## Important Constraints

- Never put real PHI in code, logs, mock data, screenshots, commits, or console output.
- Use fake or masked patient names, DOBs, phone numbers, and medication names.
- Do not log medication details or DOBs in frontend/server logs.
- Do not implement SMS unless explicitly requested again. SMS follow-up is currently not part of active work.
- Do not commit `.env`, `.env.local`, `server/.env`, `server/local.config.json`, `node_modules`, `dist`, `server/dist`, or database files.
- Keep Vercel deployment attached to the existing PharmaFlow AI project.
- Vercel production currently needs a durable Postgres `DATABASE_URL` for reliable real-call status persistence. Temporary SQLite on Vercel is demo-only.

## Twilio Notes

- `AUTO_CALL_TEST_MODE=true` simulates calls.
- `AUTO_CALL_TEST_MODE=false` places real Twilio calls.
- `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` must be public HTTPS for Twilio webhooks.
- Trial Twilio accounts can only call verified destination numbers.
- Current production public base URL should be `https://pharmaflow-ai.vercel.app`.
- Do not call real patients from test data.

## Engineering Style

- Match existing React/Tailwind/Radix patterns.
- Prefer small, scoped changes.
- Keep UI pharmacy-friendly, clear, and non-technical.
- Use loading, empty, and error states for user-facing flows.
- Make desktop and mobile layouts work.
- Run `npm run build` before deploy/commit.
- For UI QA, verify `/calls` and `/dashboard` in desktop and mobile sizes when those areas are touched.

## Deployment Workflow

1. Inspect `git status --short`.
2. Run `npm run build`.
3. Deploy with `npx vercel@latest deploy --prod --yes`.
4. Verify `https://pharmaflow-ai.vercel.app/api/health`.
5. Verify the changed production route in browser or Playwright.
6. Commit only safe files.
7. Push to `origin main`.

## Communication

When reporting back:

- Say exactly what changed.
- Say what commands passed.
- Include production URL if deployed.
- Include commit hash if committed.
- Mention remaining limitations honestly, especially database durability or Twilio trial restrictions.
